mathdb-lean problems
====================

This repository publishes benchmark releases of mathematical problems formalized
in Lean 4. Each source directory under `problems/` is also the Lean project its
problems compile against.

FORMAL CONJECTURES, REQUIRED NOT COPIED
---------------------------------------

`problems/formal-conjectures/` and `problems/mathdb-lean/` are Lean projects that
require Formal Conjectures (https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures,
Apache License, Version 2.0) as a Lake dependency, at the upstream commit their
`lakefile.toml` names, unmodified. The statement-support libraries problem
modules import, `FormalConjecturesUtil` and `FormalConjecturesForMathlib`, are
fetched from upstream by Lake under upstream's names; this repository carries no
copy of them. Their `lean-toolchain` and Mathlib revision are upstream's.

Until 2026-10-28 this repository carried a renamed copy of those two libraries
(`MathDBUtil`, `MathDBMathlib`), twelve files of it edited to build on Lean
4.34.1, and a mirror of upstream's statement corpus under `FormalConjectures/`
with one import renamed. Both were removed; this repository's history holds them.

`problems/openai-math/` is a Lean project that requires Mathlib alone, at the
revision openai/math pins.

PROBLEM STATEMENTS
------------------

The problem modules under `problems/` come from three sources, and every module
and `problem.toml` records which, with the upstream file, declaration and
revision it came from. They are generated by the mathdb-lean problem library,
which is maintained separately; this repository holds its output.

* Formal Conjectures: derived mechanically from upstream's `FormalConjectures/`
  at the revision each `problem.toml` records, across twelve of its
  directories, which is likewise Apache-2.0.

* mathdb-lean: statements written in the mathdb-lean problem library itself,
  under its `authored/`, for problems no imported corpus had formalized. They
  are this project's own work.

* openai/math (https://github.com/openai/math, Copyright 2026 OpenAI, Apache
  License, Version 2.0): derived from the Lean challenge files
  `lean/ComparatorChallenges/*.lean` at revision
  fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb. CHANGES FROM UPSTREAM: each module
  reproduces the challenge's definitions, docstrings and statements verbatim
  under the `OAI` namespace, with two marked additions -- every `sorry`-bodied
  theorem is followed by a definition of the proposition it states, its section
  variables written out, and a `Problem.Target` conjoining those propositions is
  appended for the grader. The proofs upstream keeps in its `OAI` library are
  not copied. The accompanying catalogue under `openai-math/`
  (`MANUSCRIPTS.md`, `manuscripts.json`, `CATALOGUE.json`) is compiled from that
  repository's `CONTENTS.md`, `lean/docs/*.md`, `lean/formalization.yaml` and
  `history.md`: titles, descriptions, abstracts, scope notes and withdrawal
  notices, with a link to each manuscript's PDF in that repository at that
  revision. The manuscripts themselves are not redistributed. openai/math is a
  project of OpenAI; this repository is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  OpenAI.

Formal Conjectures is a project of Google DeepMind and the Formal Conjectures
Authors, listed below. This repository is not affiliated with or endorsed by
